treatment capabilities.

606
00:40:00,780 --> 00:40:04,420
Movement of the brain
and spinal cord,

607
00:40:04,420 --> 00:40:07,580
we'll look briefly
at that movement.

608
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:13,900
And just to give you the
thought that this also is

609
00:40:13,900 --> 00:40:17,290
an area where there is the
possibility for dysfunction.

610
00:40:17,290 --> 00:40:22,900
And so a dysfunction of
the brain, I see pretty

611
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:28,260
commonly in traumatic brain
injuries. And yes, treating

612
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:31,360
the bones and membranes
to improve function,

613
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:35,840
because if you get a concussion
bad enough to give you

614
00:40:35,840 --> 00:40:39,580
a traumatic brain injury,
that is going to have a

615
00:40:39,580 --> 00:40:43,400
huge impact on the bones and
the membranes. but sometimes

616
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:48,780
it's the motility of
the brain that's a big

617
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:52,760
component. And if you can't
identify that in treatment

618
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:57,360
and treat it, you don't
entirely help your patient.

619
00:40:57,700 --> 00:41:04,060
And so motility, again, he
chose that term. The bones

620
00:41:04,060 --> 00:41:07,320
and membranes have mobility,
so they need to be moved.

621
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:12,740
Motility is capable of
moving itself. And so he did

622
00:41:12,740 --> 00:41:17,840
think there was motion that
originated from the brain.

623
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:22,840
He did not consider it
the drive of the primary

624
00:41:22,840 --> 00:41:26,800
respiratory mechanism that
is in the fluid, which

625
00:41:26,800 --> 00:41:32,360
we're about to get to. And
then when he described the

626
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:35,550
nervous system, he'd look
at embryology because

627
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:42,200
the movement of the nervous
system can be seen from

628
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:46,340
its development. So this
is early development. The

629
00:41:46,340 --> 00:41:49,960
nervous system is really
just a tube, and then it

630
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:52,400
grows this bud that's
going to become our brain.

631
00:41:52,580 --> 00:41:57,740
And that tube elongates,
but that bud at the top

632
00:41:57,740 --> 00:42:01,720
dips down. and you can see
here it dips down quite

633
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:09,920
a bit before it then these
cortical buds that are

634
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:13,340
going to become our cortex
come off and those are

635
00:42:13,340 --> 00:42:18,060
going to coil so here you
see the cortex starting to

636
00:42:18,060 --> 00:42:22,840
develop and it kind of
coils in this picture here

637
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:27,620
it is now really coiling
around um and um and here's

638
00:42:27,620 --> 00:42:31,600
that uh directionality
so the neural tube comes

639
00:42:31,600 --> 00:42:36,080
up dips down and then the
cortex comes out in coils

640
00:42:36,080 --> 00:42:40,260
and that sort of coiling
and uncoiling is the

641
00:42:40,260 --> 00:42:45,320
motion of the um of the
neural tube uh to to sort of

642
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:50,200
see it um in in function
again uh lengthening uh

643
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:54,760
dipping down and then a
coiling out of the cortex.

644
00:42:55,270 --> 00:42:58,150
And you can see that in the
shape of the ventricles.

645
00:42:58,980 --> 00:43:03,790
Here's the center of
the neural tube comes up

646
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:07,020
and I lost my arrow,
kind of coils down. And

647
00:43:07,020 --> 00:43:10,840
then this lateral ventricle
would be that coiling

648
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:15,100
or uncoiling of the
cortex as it develops.

649
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:18,300
And so during inhalation

650
00:43:18,300 --> 00:43:20,740
phase, this is going to coil.

651
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:24,300
It's going to get, the
spinal cord's going to lift

652
00:43:24,300 --> 00:43:27,660
like a tadpole's tail,
and this is going to coil

653
00:43:27,660 --> 00:43:31,340
getting kind of shorter
and fatter, the same shape

654
00:43:31,340 --> 00:43:35,040
