area, but it's fluctuation

686
00:45:30,760 --> 00:45:33,360
that's going to really
determine what's happening

687
00:45:33,360 --> 00:45:38,120
at that interstitial space,
the microcirculation,

688
00:45:38,120 --> 00:45:42,720
if you will. So the CSF
does have a circulation,

689
00:45:42,720 --> 00:45:47,580
fluid comes in at the
choroid plexus, and

690
00:45:47,580 --> 00:45:50,640
then will exit at the
arachnoid granulation.

691
00:45:50,940 --> 00:45:55,340
This is not sufficient
for all the functions

692
00:45:55,340 --> 00:45:58,580
of the CSF. And so we
can look at this concept

693
00:45:58,580 --> 00:46:01,340
of fluctuation. It
is a general concept,

694
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:05,740
heart, vascular
system, capillary beds,

695
00:46:06,220 --> 00:46:10,040
interstitium with cellular
exchange, and then

696
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:11,820
we'll look at this from
the other side. This

697
00:46:11,820 --> 00:46:14,680
is a lymphatic vessel,
but this is really

698
00:46:14,680 --> 00:46:17,990
where exchange is going
to be. And ultimately,

699
00:46:18,480 --> 00:46:23,020
the pressure in the
interstitium is negative.

700
00:46:23,580 --> 00:46:28,960
And so fluids will not
move themselves when

701
00:46:28,960 --> 00:46:32,140
faced with a negative
interstitial pressure.

702
00:46:32,140 --> 00:46:36,440
And so circulation would
bring some fluid in. But

703
00:46:36,440 --> 00:46:39,120
here where exchange is
occurring, there would be

704
00:46:39,120 --> 00:46:43,920
stasis. unless you have some
sort of action to create

